{"theorems":[{"slogan_id":10676257,"theorem_id":25939467,"name":"Lemma 7.2 (\\cite {GurevichShelah96})","body":"If $G$ is an odd and ordered bipartite graph, then $\\mathsf{MP}(G)$ is asymmetric.","slogan":"An odd and ordered bipartite graph has an asymmetric matching polytope. The polytope's asymmetry holds under these specific conditions. This result applies to graphs with the given bipartite and ordering properties.","theorem_type":"lemma","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"2210.07869v7","source":"arXiv","title":"Witnessed Symmetric Choice and Interpretations in Fixed-Point Logic with Counting","authors":["Moritz Lichter"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2210.07869v7","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"cs.LO","categories":["cs.LO","math.LO"],"citations":0,"year":2025,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.5394603127723713,"score":0.5394603127723713,"has_metadata":true},{"slogan_id":6521213,"theorem_id":21595533,"name":"Lemma 2.3","body":"Let\\/  $G$ be a non-homogeneous graph with\\/  $n$ vertices. Then there exists a non-uniform consistent random ordering that is uniform on any subset of\\/  $n-1$ vertices. Moreover it can be realised by assigning uniform\\/  $($dependent$)$ random variables\\/  $X_v\\in [0,1]$ to vertices\\/  $v\\in V(G)$ in such a way that any set of\\/  $n-1$ variables\\/  $X_v$ are independent.","slogan":"For a non-homogeneous graph with n vertices, there is a non-uniform consistent random ordering that is uniform on any subset of n minus one vertices. This ordering is achieved by assigning dependent uniform random variables in the interval from zero to one to each vertex. Any set of n minus one such variables are independent.","theorem_type":"lemma","label":null,"link":null,"paper":{"paper_id":"1506.03343v1","source":"arXiv","title":"Consistent random vertex-orderings of graphs","authors":["Paul Balister","Béla Bollobás","Svante Janson"],"link":"http://arxiv.org/abs/1506.03343v1","summary":null,"journal_ref":null,"primary_category":"math.PR","categories":["math.PR","math.CO"],"citations":0,"year":2015,"journal_published":false},"similarity":0.5258004226029047,"score":0.5258004226029047,"has_metadata":true}]}